    "triageRationale": "Small bugfix ISSUE-b902426092868097: two writers append a server section without accounting for the inline list that Vibe saves.",
    "epicSlug": "keep-vibe-configs-valid-when-registering",
    "updatedAt": "2026-11-09T07:49:56.561Z"
  },
  "body": {
    "focus": "Registering the insrc server in a Vibe config that holds a top-level inline mcp_servers list produces a valid TOML file, from both the VS Code plugin (vscode-plugin/src/hosts/toml-mcp-writer.ts) and the daemon (upsertVibeProjectServer in src/daemon/mcp-register.ts). Every server already in the inline list and every other setting is kept, and insrc is registered once. Registering again changes nothing. Where a writer cannot safely bring a config into a valid form, it leaves the file untouched and reports the failure instead of writing an invalid file.",
    "producesLld": false,
    "commit": "c571e6fe7",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "passed": false
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Both Vibe config writers now move an inline mcp_servers list into [[mcp_servers]] tables before adding the insrc server, through one shared helper, and leave a config they cannot fix untouched. Quoted and escaped spellings of the keys are recognised, and an inline entry spanning lines is refused. The user chose to keep the shared helper and accepted that an escaped server name is not recognised as insrc.",
